{"version":"1","id":"webdevcody","handle":"webdevcody","name":"Web Dev Cody","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/s--9ioIrvxf--/f_auto/v1723789220/logos/webdevcody","description":null,"is_squad":false,"x":-7.3338,"y":-9.9099,"cluster_id":3,"posts_collected":300,"newest_post_at":"2026-05-07T15:22:55.000Z","oldest_post_at":"2024-05-19T13:05:01.000Z","features":{"hype_score":0.01,"listicle_ratio":0.003333,"question_ratio":0.02,"avg_read_time":17.406667,"summary_length_avg":520.033898,"title_length_avg":50.73,"title_length_var":191.850433,"tag_entropy":3.879489,"tag_diversity":0.433333,"top_tag_share":0.153333,"avg_upvotes":8.943333,"median_upvotes":2.0,"avg_comments":0.516667,"comment_to_upvote_ratio":0.058122,"zero_engagement_share":0.346667,"viral_share":0.016667,"posts_per_week":3.336634,"non_article_ratio":1.0,"author_present_share":0.0,"recency_skew":0.123596},"view_coords":{"engagement_style":[6.8824,5.4412],"cadence_depth":[5.7647,8.4265],"hype_variety":[1.3824,6.5441],"title_style":[0.9559,0.6618]},"top_tags":[["webdev",140],["ai",76],["general-programming",65],["react",34],["ai-coding",29],["claude",29],["javascript",29],["game-development",27]],"sample_titles":{"representative":["This is the software engineering mindset you need","This is the coolest side project I've worked on","My side project now has 4 paying customers"],"outlier":["Build a Second Brain App including AI Vector Search (Next.js, Shadcn, Typescript, Convex, Clerk)"]},"recent_posts":[{"id":"RZnf6xKtM","title":"My Tips for Designing Better User Experiences","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=37Ei3f808X4","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/my-tips-for-designing-better-user-experiences-rznf6xktm","summary":"A walkthrough of UX design decisions made while building Mission Control, a developer tool for vibe coders and agentic coding workflows. Key principles covered include defining your target audience, optimizing for core workflows, using hotkeys for power users, keeping UI language simple for non-coders, and only surfacing frequently-used actions in the main UI. The author also discusses tradeoffs around features like git worktrees and pull request management, ultimately deciding to exclude them to reduce complexity for the target audience of solo vibe coders.","image":"https://i.ytimg.com/vi/37Ei3f808X4/sddefault.jpg","num_upvotes":0,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2026-05-07T15:22:55.000Z"},{"id":"FjRoM1uHr","title":"AI is killing programming tutorials and developer content creation","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=iDFcB98Z6ro","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/it-is-true-and-it-s-sad-fjrom1uhr","summary":"A developer reacts to WebDev Simplified's video about AI's impact on programming content creation. Key points: programming tutorial views are collapsing as audiences shift to AI content, YouTube ad revenue for educational channels is unsustainable ($31K/year for 2M subscribers), AI tools like Claude Code are replacing the need to watch tutorials, and there's a concerning feedback loop where AI trains on human-created content while simultaneously making that content less profitable to produce. The author argues AI coding tools are genuinely transformative (not a fad like crypto), advocates for developers to build foundational knowledge before relying on AI, and warns that software engineer salaries may decline as AI lowers the cost of building software.","image":"https://i.ytimg.com/vi/iDFcB98Z6ro/sddefault.jpg","num_upvotes":0,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2026-05-05T14:50:18.000Z"},{"id":"X5HsbvEFl","title":"Your AI Code Gets Worse Over Time \u2014 Here\u2019s What I Run","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=2u8XZwxtb9M","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/your-ai-code-gets-worse-over-time-here-s-what-i-run-x5hsbvefl","summary":null,"image":"https://i.ytimg.com/vi/2u8XZwxtb9M/sddefault.jpg","num_upvotes":0,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2026-05-04T16:10:07.000Z"},{"id":"p1tp8ypZ6","title":"Are AI Coding Skills Just Hype? I Tested Them","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=ckqO3n-4IOI","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/are-ai-coding-skills-just-hype-i-tested-them-p1tp8ypz6","summary":null,"image":"https://i.ytimg.com/vi/ckqO3n-4IOI/sddefault.jpg","num_upvotes":1,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2026-05-02T17:03:52.000Z"},{"id":"6MHeV0eNw","title":"GPT Image 2 is amazing for stock photos","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=dJa2EvFDTkk","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/gpt-image-2-is-amazing-for-stock-photos-6mhev0enw","summary":null,"image":"https://i.ytimg.com/vi/dJa2EvFDTkk/sddefault.jpg","num_upvotes":0,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2026-05-01T16:02:42.000Z"},{"id":"oUaq25oAj","title":"This Claude Skill Saves Me Hours on Every Landing Page","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=tfVAMTMUPk8","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/this-claude-skill-saves-me-hours-on-every-landing-page-ouaq25oaj","summary":null,"image":"https://i.ytimg.com/vi/tfVAMTMUPk8/sddefault.jpg","num_upvotes":0,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2026-05-01T13:36:56.000Z"},{"id":"x89h4TgDz","title":"I Didn\u2019t Expect This: Opus 4.7 vs GPT 5.5","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=p2-z1v6Zjuk","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/i-didn-t-expect-this-opus-4-7-vs-gpt-5-5-x89h4tgdz","summary":null,"image":"https://i.ytimg.com/vi/p2-z1v6Zjuk/sddefault.jpg","num_upvotes":1,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2026-04-30T16:13:12.000Z"},{"id":"nRXaPZq2v","title":"AI plugin that automates git commits and pull request descriptions","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=TpoJ044l0Q8","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/this-one-skill-eliminates-pr-busywork-nrxapzq2v","summary":"A developer showcases a custom AI-powered plugin called 'Agentic System Labs Essentials' that automates the pull request workflow. The tool analyzes staged changes, groups them into logical commits, proposes a branch name, generates a descriptive PR description, links relevant GitHub issues, suggests reviewers, and auto-tags labels. The demo walks through installing the plugin, running the 'ship PR' skill, reviewing the AI-generated commit plan, and confirming the final pull request on GitHub. The plugin requires the GitHub CLI to be authenticated and is open source.","image":"https://i.ytimg.com/vi/TpoJ044l0Q8/sddefault.jpg","num_upvotes":0,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2026-04-28T13:44:52.000Z"},{"id":"V2OGA1qjF","title":"Practical uses of GPT Image 2 for web projects and side projects","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=5JJohLtp1Ug","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/i-didn-t-expect-gpt-image-2-to-be-this-good-v2oga1qjf","summary":"A hands-on walkthrough of OpenAI's GPT Image 2 model, showcasing practical use cases including generating open graph images from website URLs, extracting and fixing perspective on phone screenshots, creating transparent cutouts, and redesigning landing page hero sections. The author demonstrates integrating Image 2 into side projects like an icon generator and an AI clip studio, highlighting the model's text rendering quality and image editing capabilities.","image":"https://i.ytimg.com/vi/5JJohLtp1Ug/sddefault.jpg","num_upvotes":0,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2026-04-26T13:49:29.000Z"},{"id":"IOOfsc26D","title":"Understanding Opus 4.7 Effort Level","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=xBfEeBAHLt4","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/understanding-opus-4-7-effort-level-ioofsc26d","summary":"A walkthrough of how effort levels work in Claude's Opus 4.7 model, based on a Reddit post. Key points: effort is a behavioral signal controlling adaptive reasoning depth, tool call appetite, response length, and agentic autonomy \u2014 not a strict token budget. Opus 4.7 defaults to 'extra high' effort on all plans including Pro, while Opus 4.6 defaulted to 'medium' on Pro/Max plans, explaining why some users perceived a quality drop. Low effort Opus 4.7 roughly equals medium effort Opus 4.6. Importantly, context quality can matter more than effort level \u2014 a well-contextualized low-effort prompt often beats a poorly-contextualized max-effort one. Opus 4.7 also uses 10\u201335% more tokens than 4.6, so matching effort level to task complexity (e.g., Sonnet low for simple tasks, Opus max for architecture/security) is important for managing token costs.","image":"https://i.ytimg.com/vi/xBfEeBAHLt4/sddefault.jpg","num_upvotes":0,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2026-04-24T12:48:19.000Z"}],"similar_handles":["dotnet","coredumpped","bytegrad","mentaloutlaw","vuemastery"],"opposite_handles":["horde","watercooler","dailydevworld","alexfinn","tbpn"],"similar":[{"id":"dotnet","handle":"dotnet","name":".NET Blog","is_squad":false,"x":-7.2879,"y":-9.7322,"cluster_id":3,"posts_collected":462,"image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/t_logo,f_auto/v1/logos/f23eb59371bd4f07aeef64c4eef73266","features_preview":{"posts_per_week":2.726935,"median_upvotes":1.0,"author_present_share":0.0,"hype_score":0.031385,"avg_read_time":21.835498,"tag_diversity":0.324675},"top_tags_preview":[[".net",389],["c#",91],["ai",91]],"view_coords":{"engagement_style":[3.2647,-0.0147],"cadence_depth":[8.2353,8.8824],"hype_variety":[6.8824,5.1029],"title_style":[6.2647,-7.3971]}},{"id":"coredumpped","handle":"coredumpped","name":"Core Dumped","is_squad":false,"x":-7.1665,"y":-9.6029,"cluster_id":3,"posts_collected":43,"image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/s--N9ie6ehW--/f_auto/v1725038034/logos/coredumpped","features_preview":{"posts_per_week":0.514627,"median_upvotes":1.0,"author_present_share":0.0,"hype_score":0.0,"avg_read_time":16.325581,"tag_diversity":0.604651},"top_tags_preview":[["computer-science",11],["rust",7],["c",7]],"view_coords":{"engagement_style":[3.3382,-1.9559],"cadence_depth":[-5.1471,8.2647],"hype_variety":[-8.7794,-3.1176],"title_style":[9.0588,-8.0588]}},{"id":"bytegrad","handle":"bytegrad","name":"ByteGrad","is_